:name: dya2 right-trackball -- Studio over USB CDC + simulated PMW3610 trackball
:description: Boot the real dya2 studio-rpc-usb-uart image (central-only) with a
:description: simulated PMW3610 on SPIM0. console on uart0, uart1 idle (real image
:description: speaks Studio over USB CDC). No `start`/NVS preload here -- renode_serve.py
:description: issues them over the monitor after connecting the UART sockets.

# Local (vendored) variant of zmk-west-commands' platforms/single_real.resc.
# The only difference is $platform: renode_serve.py materializes the combined
# USB+PMW3610 repl (xiao_nrf52840_usb_pmw3610.repl) with absolute model paths
# and passes it here. Everything else -- VectorTableOffset at the UF2 load
# offset, the two UART server sockets -- matches single_real.resc so the same
# boot_single_real-style sequence (LoadBinary FF NVS, then start) applies.

using sysbus

$bin?=@zmk.elf
$console_port?=3455
$rpc_port?=3456
$platform?=@platforms/xiao_nrf52840_usb_pmw3610.repl
# xiao_ble//zmk links at the Adafruit-UF2 bootloader offset
# (CONFIG_FLASH_LOAD_OFFSET); the reset vector is there, not at 0x0.
$vtor?=0x27000

mach create "dya2"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $platform

emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal $console_port "console_term" false
connector Connect sysbus.uart0 console_term

emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal $rpc_port "rpc_term" false
connector Connect sysbus.uart1 rpc_term

sysbus LoadELF $bin
sysbus.cpu VectorTableOffset $vtor
